# Office lock files (created when a .pptx/.docx is open in PowerPoint/Word)
~$*
# Radar prompt-compression reports (generated on-demand from Debug panel)
report/

# Python bytecode cache (e.g. from running tools/*.py)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# macOS Finder metadata — should never be tracked
.DS_Store
.claude/

# Security remediation work-orders (list unfixed vulns — never publish to the public repo)
security-remediation-*.md
server/ca-key.pem
server/ca-cert.pem
server/ca-cert.srl
server/leaf.csr
server/leaf-ext.conf
settings.json.bak
settings.json.tmp
settings.json.*.tmp

# GitHub traffic archiver (tools/track-traffic.sh) — local-only artefacts.
# The SCRIPT itself stays tracked on purpose (maintainer tool, like the rest of
# tools/); what must never land in the repo is its state. Defensive by design:
# the defaults all live outside the working tree (~/.config, ~/.local/share),
# but GH_TOKEN_FILE and OUT are overridable, so a redirected run must not be
# able to stage a PAT. The launchd plist is machine-specific (absolute paths).
gh-token
gh-token.*
traffic-history.csv
track-traffic.log
com.pi-weather-station.traffic.plist
